hnicity stratifies the lives of individuals in the U.S.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(SBA-AS, SCD-AS, SSC-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-SBY)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2846, "crseId": 370853, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "AMST", "catalogNbr": "2371", "titleShort": "Global Hip Hop", "titleLong": "Planet Rap: Where Hip Hop Came From and Where It's Going", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1168, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "05/30/2023", "endDt": "06/16/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 5, "netid": "cma249", "firstName": "Catherine", "middleName": "M.", "lastName": "Appert"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Online Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=3335"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "05/30/2023", "endDt": "06/16/2023", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "AD", "instrModeDescrshort": "DL-AD", "instrModeDescr": "Distance Learning-Asynchronous", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "ASRC", "catalogNbr": "2370", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "MUSIC", "catalogNbr": "2370", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "3W1", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2023", "sessionEndDt": "06/16/2023", "sessionLong": "Three Week - First", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "Since hip hop first emerged in the South Bronx nearly half a century ago, it has grown into a global movement. Youth around the world not only consume hip hop; they also create their own, adapting hip hop music, texts, dance, and visual culture to local realities. This course traces the ongoing connections between hip hop's roots in the cultural expression of marginalized African American and Latinx youth in the postindustrial urban United States, its contemporary relationship to US popular culture, and its routes around the globe, where diverse practitioners mobilize its beats, rhymes, and visual culture to address experiences of oppression and displacement, celebrate life, and agitate for social justice.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(ALC-AS, CA-AS, SCD-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "Forbidden Overlap: due to an overlap in content, students will receive credit for only one course in the following group: AMST 2371, ASRC 2370, MUSIC 2370, MUSIC 3490.", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Winter, Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2846, "crseId": 359630, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "AMST", "catalogNbr": "3071", "titleShort": "Enduring Global & Amer Issues", "titleLong": "Enduring Global and American Issues", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1907, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "06:30PM", "timeEnd": "10:00PM", "startDt": "06/05/2023", "endDt": "07/28/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 5, "netid": "ds90", "firstName": "David", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Silbey"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "To Be Assigned", "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": "TBA", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Taught in Washington, DC. This Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=3541"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "DC", "locationDescr": "Washington, DC", "startDt": "06/05/2023", "endDt": "07/28/2023", "addConsent": "I", "addConsentDescr": "Instructor Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "GOVT", "catalogNbr": "3071", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "PAM", "catalogNbr": "3071", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "SP2", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2023", "sessionEndDt": "08/19/2023", "sessionLong": "Summer Special Session 2", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "The US and the global community face a number of complex, interconnected and enduring issues that pose challenges for our political and policy governance institutions and society at large.\u00a0 Exploring how the US and the world conceive of the challenges and take action on them is fundamental to understanding them.\u00a0 This course investigates such issues, especially ones that fit into the critically important areas of sustainability, social justice, technology, public health and globalization, security and conflict, among others. Students will engage with these areas and issues and the challenges they pose, using multiple frameworks and approaches, through weekly class discussions and lectures.\"", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(GLC-AS, SBA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring, Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2846, "crseId": 351417, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "AMST", "catalogNbr": "3141", "titleShort": "Prisons", "titleLong": "Prisons", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1249, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "05/30/2023", "endDt": "06/16/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 4, "netid": "mcs378", "firstName": "Matthew", "middleName": "C", "lastName": "Saleh"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "This Online Summer Session class is offered by the School of Continuing Education and Summer Sessions. For details visit http://www.sce.cornell.edu/ss/courses/courses.php?v=1883"}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "05/30/2023", "endDt": "06/16/2023", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "AD", "instrModeDescrshort": "DL-AD", "instrModeDescr": "Distance Learning-Asynchronous", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "GOVT", "catalogNbr": "3141", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "3W1", "sessionBeginDt": "05/30/2023", "sessionEndDt": "06/16/2023", "sessionLong": "Three Week - First", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "The United States stands alone among Western, industrialized countries with its persistent, high rates of incarceration, long sentences, and continued use of the death penalty. This \"American exceptionalism\" -- the turn to mass incarceration -- has been fostered by the use of sharply-delineated categories that define vast numbers of people as outlaws and others as law-abiding. These categories that are based on ideas of personal responsibility and\u00a0assumptions about race are modified somewhat by a liberal commitment to human rights.\u00a0\u00a0 Our purpose in this course is to understand how such ideas have taken root and to locate the consequences of these ideas for policy and practice.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(SBA-AS, SSC-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Winter, Summer.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}]}, "message": null, "meta": {"copyright": "Cornell University, Office of the University Registrar", "rosterDttm": "2023-09-19T17:23:31-0400", "catalogDttm": "2023-09-19T16:43:39-0400"}}